RED. Two tests, both failing.

`manager-archetypes.js` no longer throws when `league_season_teams` is
absent: `leagueHistoryState()` reports the table and `archetypesFor()`
returns an empty map. So the narrowed catch on this route is now a branch
nothing can reach, and the state it used to set is no longer set at all —
the page reports `present` on a database that cannot look up a single
manager.

The tests now ask for the shape the new module makes possible: `read_state`
from `leagueHistoryState()`, and `read_reason` carrying that module's own
sentence instead of `read_failed` carrying an exception message this route
wrote about itself. A stamp, and a state, must describe the store, not the
reader.

RED: 27 tests, 25 pass, 2 fail (test/manager-signals-api.test.js).

